-- BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 probe 2 (2026-10-26, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000266 BREACH-DOCTOR-1 and 1000397; ANTIFRAGILE-1: an alternate is judged by whether it ran, never by the health of the path it backs up).
-- Follow-up of migrations/2026-10-26-breach-doctor-watch.sql (PR 4583, merged, migration_runs id 614, ok at 2026-10-26T11:17:30Z). That file is not edited (MIGRATION-NO-CLOBBER-1); this one replaces one probe.
-- Defect found in review of the merged package: the spof_alternate_probes row of 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' judged the alternate by two things, a breach-doctor-watch event inside 30 minutes and
-- doctor_tick_age_min at 30 or below. The second clause measures the doctor, the path the watch backs up, so the probe failed exactly when the alternate did its job: during a real stall the watch files the stall
-- issue, its event reads status ok, and the same run writes doctor_tick_age_min = 47, so the drill (chaosDrill every 360 minutes, chaosJudge in qnfo-fleet-control) saw 'doctor_tick_age_min reads 47 minutes, above the
-- limit of 30', failed the alternate and filed CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 saying the alternate showed no evidence. When it did pass it proved only a live watch plus a healthy doctor. Reproduced with the real job and the
-- real chaosJudge: healthy doctor -> drill ok, doctor tick 47 minutes old with the watch alive -> watch ok/stalled/file-issue, one issue, event status ok, drill fail. The orchestrator spec's closing probe was the
-- heartbeat only; the metric limit was an addition of the first package.
-- State read 2026-10-26T11:22Z (SELECT only): the old probe is still on D1 (spof_alternate_probes, enabled, never run: last_run_at NULL), spof_registry alternate_tested_at is NULL, the watch is deployed (cloud_ops_events
-- breach-doctor-watch-tick, status ok, 11:20:55Z) and metric_registry doctor_tick_age_min reads 11 with last_refreshed 2026-10-26T11:20:55Z (metric_registry.last_refreshed holds three timestamp shapes across the registry, with a
-- space, with a T and Z, with milliseconds, so the probe compares julianday values and not strings; an unparsable value reads NULL and fails the probe).
-- What this file does (two guarded UPDATEs and one decision_log row, nothing deleted, alternate_tested_at never written):
--   * spof_alternate_probes: the metric clauses are replaced by one liveness clause that does not depend on the doctor's health: doctor_tick_age_min must have been refreshed (by anyone) inside 30 minutes. The ledger clause
--     and the status = ok heartbeat clause stay. The heartbeat is the proof that the watch itself ran, so a dead watch with a healthy doctor still fails (the doctor refreshes the metric, the heartbeat does not exist), a
--     stalled doctor with a live watch passes (the watch refreshes the metric from the stale tick and the heartbeat is ok), and a metric nobody refreshed in 30 minutes fails with its reason. The window_note keeps the
--     prefix the Rollback of the first file keys on and says that a stall the watch has reported counts as the alternate being exercised. Guarded by the clause text it replaces, so a replay is a no-op.
--   * spof_registry: one sentence is appended to the evidence of the doctor tick row (and its stale clause about the metric limit is brought in line): the stamp means the detect-and-report half is alive, not that the
--     diagnosis path has a second runner; issue 1000397 stays the acting half. control_registry breach-doctor-switch stays untested for the same reason, so both outcomes now agree.
--   * decision_log: one row.
-- Not in this file: the worker (qnfo-cloud-ops 1.39.0 is unchanged), the failure mode and fm- detector of the first file (they read the heartbeat only), issue 1000397 (stays open, its probe reads the acting half).
-- spof-review: no new cron, worker, binding or table.
-- charter-pillar: autonomy.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE spof_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''table'' AND name = ''breach_diagnosis_events'') THEN ''the doctor ledger breach_diagnosis_events does not exist, so there is no doctor tick to watch yet'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''breach-doctor-watch'' AND status = ''ok'' AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-30 minutes'')) THEN ''no breach-doctor-watch event answered in 30 minutes, so the second path of the breach doctor has not run'' WHEN (SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_tick_age_min'') IS NULL THEN ''doctor_tick_age_min has no value'' WHEN CAST((SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_tick_age_min'') AS REAL) > 30 THEN ''doctor_tick_age_min reads '' || (SELECT last_value FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_tick_age_min'') || '' minutes, above the limit of 30'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', window_note = replace('30 minutes for the watch heartbeat (qnfo-cloud-ops writes one breach-doctor-watch event on every 10-minute tick, three ticks of margin) and 30 minutes for the doctor tick age (doctor_tick_age_min, written by the watch from the doctor''s own tick events)@@ the watch is the exercise: it runs on every tick, so the alternate is run, not declared', '@@', char(59)) WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' AND instr(probe_sql, 'doctor_tick_age_min was not refreshed in 30 minutes') > 0; UPDATE spof_registry SET evidence = replace(replace(evidence, ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 probe 2 2026-10-26: the drill reads that the watch ran and refreshed doctor_tick_age_min and never the value of the metric, so a stall the watch has reported still passes, and a stamp means the detect-and-report half is alive and not that the diagnosis path has a second runner (issue 1000397 stays the acting half)', ''), 'which reads a breach-doctor-watch event inside 30 minutes and a refresh of doctor_tick_age_min inside 30 minutes', 'which reads a breach-doctor-watch event inside 30 minutes and doctor_tick_age_min at 30 or below') WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' AND instr(evidence, 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 probe 2 2026-10-26') > 0
-- Rollback note: the decision_log row stays (append-only); an alternate_tested_at that a passing drill stamped stays (it was earned by a drill that ran the alternate).

UPDATE spof_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sqlite_master WHERE type = ''table'' AND name = ''breach_diagnosis_events'') THEN ''the doctor ledger breach_diagnosis_events does not exist, so there is no doctor tick to watch yet'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''breach-doctor-watch'' AND status = ''ok'' AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-30 minutes'')) THEN ''no breach-doctor-watch event answered in 30 minutes, so the second path of the breach doctor has not run'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''doctor_tick_age_min'' AND julianday(last_refreshed) > julianday(''now'', ''-30 minutes'')) THEN ''doctor_tick_age_min was not refreshed in 30 minutes'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed',
  window_note = '30 minutes for the watch heartbeat (qnfo-cloud-ops writes one breach-doctor-watch event on every 10-minute tick, three ticks of margin) and 30 minutes for the doctor_tick_age_min refresh (the watch writes it on the same tick from the doctor''s own tick events, and the probe reads that it was refreshed, never its value, so a stalled doctor with a live watch passes: a stall the watch has reported counts as the alternate being exercised)'
WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' AND instr(probe_sql, 'above the limit of 30') > 0;

UPDATE spof_registry SET evidence = replace(evidence, 'which reads a breach-doctor-watch event inside 30 minutes and doctor_tick_age_min at 30 or below', 'which reads a breach-doctor-watch event inside 30 minutes and a refresh of doctor_tick_age_min inside 30 minutes') || ' | BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 probe 2 2026-10-26: the drill reads that the watch ran and refreshed doctor_tick_age_min and never the value of the metric, so a stall the watch has reported still passes, and a stamp means the detect-and-report half is alive and not that the diagnosis path has a second runner (issue 1000397 stays the acting half)'
WHERE component = 'breach doctor tick (qnfo-fleet-control */10)' AND instr(evidence, 'BREACH-DOCTOR-WATCH-1 probe 2 2026-10-26') = 0;

